Journey: The partner API enforces OAuth2 scopes
Id: api-authorization
Tags: @api @security @regression
Risk: 5
Requirements: SEC-2, SEC-3

# No token at all
Call API "GET ${API_URL}/v1/claims/CLM-100001" with errors allowed and store as anonymous
Expect the anonymous response status is 401
Capture the header "www-authenticate" of anonymous as challenge
Expect ${challenge} contains "Bearer"

# The reporting partner may read but not write
Call API "GET ${API_URL}/v1/claims/CLM-100001" as reporting and store as readOnly
Expect the readOnly response status is 200
Call API "POST ${API_URL}/v1/claims" with body '{"policyId":"POL-H-100231","type":"WATER","incidentDate":"2026-10-01","amountClaimed":100,"description":"Scope test, must be refused"}' as reporting and store as write
Expect the write response status is 403
Expect response write "$.error" equals "insufficient_scope"
Call API "POST ${API_URL}/v1/batch/jobs" with body '{"businessDate":"2026-10-23"}' as reporting and store as batch
Expect the batch response status is 403

# A wrong client secret gets no token
Call API "POST ${API_URL}/oauth/token" with form grant_type=client_credentials, client_id=broker-gateway, client_secret=wrong and store as badToken
Expect the badToken response status is 401
Expect response badToken "$.error" equals "invalid_client"
